Raitchi license map

The default Raitchi engine distribution includes GPL-3.0-or-later components
adapted from Eden/yuzu, including kernel thread affinity and audio-renderer
work-size accounting. The Eden-derived Android shell is GPL-3.0-or-later.
The unmodified GNU GPL version 3 license text is provided in COPYING.

Individual source-file notices and retained upstream grants remain authoritative.
In particular, the MIT-licensed LAS Recomp, Let's Go Recomp and Echoes-derived
parts retain their MIT grants and original copyright notices. This license map
does not replace those notices or relicense third-party files.

Full component notices:
- ports/shared-android/runtime/LICENSE-kernel-thread-affinity.txt
- ports/shared-android/runtime/services/LICENSE-audren-work-size.txt
- native/runtime/LICENSE-LASRecomp
- native/runtime/LICENSE-LetsGo
- native/runtime/LICENSE-Echoes
- native/runtime/LICENSE-EoWRecomp
- native/adapters/echoes/LICENSE
- ports/letsgo-android/LICENSE-AdrenoTools
- ports/letsgo-android/LICENSE-LinkerNSBypass
- ports/shared-android/assets/fonts/OFL-Fredoka.txt
- ports/shared-android/assets/fonts/LICENSE-ButtonGlyphs.txt

See NOTICE.md for source provenance, build configurations and dependency notices.
The separate shell retains its own LICENSE.txt and per-file notices.

The default release configuration excludes the optional Unicorn native-blocks
backend and legacy on-device compiler toolkit. Their separate licenses and
packaged notices must be retained when either option is enabled. This document
makes no blanket license-compatibility claim for every optional configuration.
